0212: blueline OS-initiated cluster idle (bluecpu_idle=3, off by default)

Step 1 toward the apps subsystem's RPMh sleep: PSCI OS-initiated mode with
Linux's sdm845 states (cores 0x40000004, the last one 0x4100c244), and the
earliest deadline in the apps RSC's CONTROL TCS so the AOSS wakes the APSS.

bluecpu_idle_ss (bits, off by default): the apps RSC's sleep/wake sets.
1 = MC0, SH0, MM0-3 at 0 in sleep; 2 = xo.lvl 0; 4 = cx.lvl and mx.lvl at
level index 0 (wake: first level >= NOM). The sleep TCS is enabled only
while the panel sleeps (from blue_bw_park, 0211; armed with the panel on,
the phone hung within ~25 s), and the last core skips the cluster state
while a UFS command is in flight. Every 10 s it also logs the AOP's SoC
sleep counters (AOSD, CXSD; msg RAM 0xc3f0000 + 0x48, as qcom_stats).

Result: stable, no change in draw (209-216 mA screen off with any set).
AOSD and CXSD stay at 0, also with GPU, Wi-Fi and sound off.

bluetimers=1 (diagnostic): every 10 s, the timers that fired most (timer
calls, thread calls, and threads' wait timeouts by process), from hooks in
timer_call.c and thread_call.c.

